<section class="section problem-section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="problem-grid fade-up">
      <div class="problem-heading">
        <h2>The Gaps That Hurt Agencies Are Almost Always the Ones Nobody Was Looking For</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-body">
        <div class="accent-bar"></div>
        <p>Independent agencies run lean. That means tech stacks that get set up once and forgotten. Security settings from a previous employee. A website that used to convert leads but stopped somewhere along the way. Tools that are paid for but not actually used.</p>
        <p class="pull-quote">None of it feels like a crisis &mdash; until it is.</p>
        <p>Carrier cyber requirements are tightening. Compliance expectations are increasing. And the agencies that get caught flat-footed aren&rsquo;t the ones ignoring the problem on purpose &mdash; they&rsquo;re the ones who just never had a clear picture of where they stood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem-section {
    background: var(--light-bg);
  }

  .problem-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .problem-heading h2 {
    text-align: left;
  }

  .accent-bar {
    width: 48px;
    height: 3px;
    background: var(--orange);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .problem-body p {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-light);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .problem-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .problem-body p.pull-quote {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--orange);
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 28px 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .problem-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
